  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 138 AM EDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\n- Low chance of Rain on Saturday\n\nSurface high pressure moves east on Saturday and return flow \nbrings some moisture. There could be a few showers on Saturday \nand Saturday night. There is enough ensemble support to bump up\nNBM POPs from around zero to slight/low chance across the northern\nzones where the better moisture and lift is located.\n\n- Showers and Thunderstorms Possible Late Monday into Tuesday\n\nA shortwave trough ejects out of the northern Rockies with a\nsurface low tracking into Canada early next week. A trailing cold\nfront is expected to touch off showers and thunderstorms Monday\nnight and Tuesday. Instability and deeper moisture is across \nnorthern Lower Michigan pooling ahead of the cold front, which \nsinks south through the forecast area on Tuesday. Precipitable \nwater surges close 2 inches, so heavy rain potential is there as \nthe front will be moving slowly and MBE vectors are less than 10 \nknots.\n\nThe front stalls across the southern zones on Wednesday, with a\nrainy stretch of weather possible through Thursday as a surface \nlow tracks along the front across southern Lower Michigan.",
